      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. Let me analyze it:\n\n1. Gets the default `LevenshteinDistance` (unlimited) instance\n2. Creates `charBuffer0` = `\")\\u0000\"` (char array `[')', '\\0']`)\n3. Computes distance between `charBuffer0` and itself → result is `0` (identical strings), stored as `integer0`\n4. Creates `charBuffer1` = `\"\\u0000\\u0000\"` (char array `['\\0', '\\0']`)\n5. Creates a threshold-limited `LevenshteinDistance` with threshold `0`\n6. Computes distance between `charBuffer0` and `charBuffer1` with threshold `0` → they differ at position 0, actual distance `1 > 0`, so returns `-1`\n7. Asserts result is `-1`\n\nNow I'll write the improved, understandable version.The improved test compiled successfully."
